  "base_commit": "6d4184492403311f7fb7157e06788c3eb10ba60d",
  "pr_number": 5744,
  "issue_number": 5740,
  "issue_title": "parser: compound-subject additive type static silently drops the 'spell' stack-scoping (Secret Arcade)",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\n`Secret Arcade`'s additive-type static \u2014 `Nonland permanents you control and permanent spells you control are enchantments in addition to their other types.` \u2014 silently **mis-parses**, not strict-fails. The compound-subject split itself already works (`parse_continuous_subject_filter` \u2192 `parse_shared_controller_compound_subject_filter` correctly produces an `Or` of the two `you control` conjuncts), but the second conjunct, `permanent spells you control`, loses its \"spell\" qualifier entirely and resolves to a bare `Typed{Permanent, controller: You}` filter \u2014 identical to `permanents you control`.\n\nVerified Oracle text (Scryfall, `Secret Arcade // Dusty Parlor`, DSC #10):\n> Nonland permanents you control and permanent spells you control are enchantments in addition to their other types.\n\n## Root cause\n`crates/engine/src/parser/oracle_target.rs` already has a fully-built, tested mechanism for exactly this class of phrase \u2014 a bare \"spell\"/\"spells\" head noun means the filter targets an object **on the stack** (CR 109.2), not a permanent:\n- `target_phrase_mentions_spell_word` / `target_phrase_uses_spell_suffix` detect the word.\n- `scope_spell_targets_to_stack` / `stack_spell_filter` rewrite a `Typed` filter into `TargetFilter::StackSpell` (or `And{[StackSpell, Typed]}` when other type/controller constraints remain).\n- `scope_target_spell_phrase` is the entry point, wired into `parse_target_with_ctx` at two call sites (`oracle_target.rs:984`, `:1671`) \u2014 this is why targeting grammar (\"target artifact or enchantment **spell**\") already resolves correctly to a stack-scoped filter.\n\n`parse_type_phrase_with_ctx` (`oracle_target.rs:2038`) \u2014 the type-phrase grammar used by static-ability **subject** resolution \u2014 never calls `scope_target_spell_phrase`. `crates/engine/src/parser/oracle_static/shared.rs`'s `parse_continuous_subject_filter` falls through to `parse_type_phrase(subject)` at its generic fallback (`shared.rs:4305`) for any \"you control\"-suffixed conjunct not caught by an earlier special case. Since \"permanent spells you control\" hits that exact fallback, the \"spells\" head noun is silently swallowed by the bare type grammar instead of being scoped to the stack.\n\nNet effect: the static's `affected` `Or` filter becomes `[NonlandPermanentsYouControl, PermanentsYouControl]`, which collapses to \"permanents you control\" \u2014 i.e. Secret Arcade incorrectly makes **lands** you control enchantments too (never intended), and never actually reaches permanent spells on the stack at all (its real, intended effect).\n\n## Why this isn't new engine plumbing\nThe runtime side is already fully generic and stack-aware:\n- `crates/engine/src/game/layers.rs`'s `apply_continuous_effect_filtered` scans `effect.affected_filter.extract_in_zone().unwrap_or(Zone::Battlefield)` via `zone_cache.ids_for(state, scan_zone)`.\n- `crates/engine/src/game/targeting.rs:2172` \u2014 `zone_object_ids` already returns `state.stack.iter().map(|e| e.id)` for `Zone::Stack`.\n- `crates/engine/src/game/filter.rs:1796` \u2014 `filter_inner` (used by `matches_target_filter`, the matcher `apply_continuous_effect_filtered` calls) already dispatches `TargetFilter::StackSpell` / `TargetFilter::StackAbility` to `matches_stack_target_filter`.\n\nSo once the parser emits the correct `TargetFilter::StackSpell`-based conjunct, the existing continuous-effect layer application should apply it correctly with no new runtime code \u2014 this is a parser-only fix mirroring the compound-subject-dispatcher generalizations already merged in #5219 / #5406 (reuse an existing, narrowly-wired building block across a broader class of callers), except the failure mode here is a **silent semantic loss** rather than a strict-fail/`Unimplemented`.\n\n## Relevant CR\n- CR 109.2 \u2014 a bare \"spell\" head noun refers to an object on the stack.\n- CR 110.4b \u2014 \"permanent spell\" = an artifact, battle, creature, enchantment, or planeswalker spell.\n- CR 611.3a \u2014 a continuous effect generated by a static ability applies to whatever its text indicates, not just the battlefield.\n- CR 205.1b \u2014 additive type grant (\"in addition to their other types\").\n\n## Proposed fix\nExpose `scope_target_spell_phrase` (or an equivalent `pub(crate)` wrapper) from `oracle_target.rs`, and apply it at `parse_continuous_subject_filter`'s generic `parse_type_phrase` fallback in `oracle_static/shared.rs`, mirroring the two existing `parse_target_with_ctx` call sites. No existing GitHub issue covers this card or this gap.\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-13T18:09:40.000Z",
